WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.037
Choose storage according to persistence and access patterns.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:11.899
An instance's ephemeral disk may provide fast temporary workspace but can disappear when the instance is deleted.

00:00:11.899 --> 00:00:18.911
Persistent block disks survive independently and are useful for reusable environments, caches, and active data.

00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:28.473
Object storage supports durable datasets, model artifacts, and results at scale, but applications may need to stage files locally for performance.

00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:37.185
Model caches reduce repeated downloads and provisioning time, yet they generate storage charges and may contain multiple large versions.

00:00:37.185 --> 00:00:45.047
Define which artifacts are authoritative, how their integrity is verified, and when old cache entries are removed.

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:51.210
Snapshots simplify recovery, but uncontrolled snapshot growth creates both cost and data-retention risk.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:57.372
Back up configuration and irreplaceable data, then test restoration onto a clean environment.

00:00:57.372 --> 00:01:02.259
Classify datasets, prompts, outputs, embeddings, and logs before uploading them.

00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:08.421
Prompts can contain credentials, source code, personal data, regulated records, or business plans.

00:01:08.421 --> 00:01:17.558
Select approved accounts and regions, restrict access, encrypt data in transit and at rest, and understand who controls encryption keys.

00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:24.145
Minimize collection and avoid logging complete prompts by default when operational metrics would suffice.

00:01:24.145 --> 00:01:28.183
Define retention and deletion for every data class.

00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:35.620
Deleting a compute instance does not necessarily delete attached disks, snapshots, object versions, logs, or backups.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:41.782
Conversely, automatic cleanup can destroy required evidence or results if ownership is unclear.

00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:47.094
Maintain an inventory that links storage to a project and owner.

00:01:47.094 --> 00:01:59.206
Privacy-conscious cloud GPU use means knowing where data enters, where copies remain, who can access them, and how they are removed at the end of the workload.
